{"records":[{"id":"s3jtdhjdbs","title":"Supplementary data for Michaelis et al., 'Protein import motor complex reacts to mitochondrial misfolding by reducing protein import and activating mitophagy'","description":"Supplementary data for Michaelis et al., 'Mitochondrial import loss induces mitophagy without membrane depolarization'. We hypothesized that inhibition of mitochondrial protein import induced mitophagy independent of mitochondrial depolarization. This dataset contains raw Illumina sequencing data for all samples from a genome-wide CRISPR/Cas9 screen for mitophagy regulators. The genome-wide library is Brunello from Doench et al Nat Biotechnol. 2016. We found that the pre-sequence translocase-associated motor complex PAM controls mitophagy induction. Loss of PAM caused a loss in protein import and was sufficient to induce mitophagy without depolarization.\nThe samples have been sequenced on an Illumina NextSeq 500 in single end mode with 75+8 cycles. ","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-08-05T15:38:53.752Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/s3jtdhjdbs","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/s3jtdhjdbs"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jonas","last_name":"Michaelis","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Melinda","last_name":"Brunstein","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Süleyman","last_name":"Bozkurt","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Ludovico","last_name":"Alves","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Martin","last_name":"Wegner","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Manuel","last_name":"Kaulich","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Pohl","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Christian","last_name":"Münch","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Proteomics","Mitochondrion","Mitophagy","Genetic Screening","Next Generation Sequencing","CRISPR/Cas9"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"f5tf9rcxgc","title":"Sandall_Thesis_Videos","description":"Christina Sandall Doctoral Thesis Supplemental Videos. Includes representative videos of 1000 ns molecular dynamic simulation analyses of the Nucleotide-Binding Domain and Leucine-Rich Repeat-Containing Gene Family, Pyrin Domain Containing protein 3 (NLRP3) bound with ADP or ATP.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-07-21T09:22:23.58Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/f5tf9rcxgc","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/f5tf9rcxgc"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Christina","last_name":"Sandall","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Justin","last_name":"MacDonald","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Molecular Dynamics","NLRP3 Inflammasome"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"b49tkfjcm5","title":"SLC35B1 is AXER, an ATP/ADP exchanger in the ER membrane and part of a regulatory circuit","description":"The endoplasmic reticulum (ER) requires a constant ATP supply. However, the carrier that catalyzes ATP uptake into the ER was unknown. In search of the elusive ATP/ADP carrier we screened gene expression datasets for member(s) of the family of solute carriers that are co-expressed with BiP, the major ER resident ATP consumer, and are ER membrane proteins. We identified SLC35B1 as a potential candidate. Heterologous expression of SLC35B1 in E. coli revealed that SLC35B1 is highly specific for ATP and ADP and acts in antiport mode. Moreover, siRNA mediated depletion of SLC35B1 from HeLa cells reduced ER ATP levels and BiP activity. Thus, human SLC35B1 provides ATP to the ER and was named AXER (ATP/ADP exchanger in the ER membrane). Furthermore, we began to unravel an ER to cytosol low energy response regulatory axis (termed lowER) that is central for maintaining ER ATP supply under steady state and stress conditions. \n\nThis work is about to be published under the title\nAXER is an ATP/ADP exchanger in the membrane of the endoplasmic reticulum\nby\nMarie-Christine Klein, Katharina Zimmermann, Stefan Schorr, Martina Landini, Patrick A. W. Klemens, Jacqueline Altensell, Martin Jung, Elmar Krause, Duy Nguyen, Volkhard Helms, Jens Rettig, Claudia Fecher-Trost, Adolfo Cavalié, Markus Hoth, Ivan Bogeski, H. Ekkehard Neuhaus, Richard Zimmermann, Sven Lang and Ilka Haferkamp\n\nHere we present the original western blot data.","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2018-08-28T13:47:04.482Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/b49tkfjcm5","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/b49tkfjcm5"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Richard","last_name":"Zimmermann","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Marie-Christine","last_name":"Klein","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Biochemistry","Endoplasmic Reticulum","Energy Supply"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"kfr5bnzrmw","title":"LDHU3_07.0720","description":"mitochondrial ADP/ATP carrier | MCP15\nLeishmania donovani (HU3 strain)","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2022-01-18T21:22:33.704Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/kfr5bnzrmw","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/kfr5bnzrmw"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jose M.","last_name":"Requena","orcid":null},{"first_name":"Jose C.","last_name":"Solana","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Gene","Protein","Leishmania"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"2ngxychzsm","title":"LINF_070010800","description":"mitochondrial ADP/ATP carrier | MCP15; Leishmania infantum\n","source":{"id":"7377952c-6404-4428-bbfc-77242cfc301e","name":"Mendeley Data","external":false},"publication_date":"2021-01-22T18:09:01.775Z","url":"https://data.mendeley.com/datasets/2ngxychzsm","data_type":"dataset","access":"open","doi":["10.17632/2ngxychzsm"],"contributors":[{"first_name":"Jose M.","last_name":"Requena","orcid":null}],"funders":[],"categories":["Gene","Protein","Leishmania"],"journal_issn":[]},{"id":"js59hr22jn","title":"L